We can use #649 to make our addin better. We can extract `base_indention` from the text to style. Eg in 
```r 
function(...) {
  X=1
}
```
Highlighting  only `. . X=1`And styling it currently removes intention of the expression and we’d be left with

```r 
function(...) {
X <- 1
}
```

Deriving the base indention from `  X=1` would give us

```r 
function(...) {
  X <- 1
}
```

Hence, the addin would now return correct intention of any expression, not just the ones with base indention 0, as of now. 

Note that #649 was implanted because of https://github.com/r-lib/styler/issues/641, which was opened because in language server, they wanted the “addin” to preserve initial intention. So all I propose here is just to make use of the styler programmatic API they way it was done for vs Code.

